{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1170415-new-devotion-cry-for-the-hungry-horde","id":1170415,"title":"New Devotion: Cry For the Hungry Horde","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-25T06:31:24-08:00","id":1170415,"title":"New Devotion: Cry For the Hungry Horde","content":"Well here is a devotion i cooked up earlier. It belongs in my chronicle to a ancient elder blood goddess that's worshiped by the CoC. <br /> Feel free to use, critique or whatever you feel like.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cry For the Hungry Horde<br /> (Animalism \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022\u2022\u2022, Protean \u2022)<br /> Ritual burials is more then just a way of getting rid of the dead,<br /> it\u2019s a cleaning ritual that in many cultures is a way of making sure<br /> the dead stays dead. This devotion wakes the hungry dead for a short<br /> while, upsetting their sleep and fills their dead bodies with a<br /> mockery of kindred powers, not dead but neither Kindred.<br /> This Devotion costs 4 experience to learn.<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10 vitae<br /> <b>Dice pool: </b>Intelligence + Occult + Animalism<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> To activate this Devotion, the vampire spills his Vitae over an area, no larger then a small cemetery,<br /> filled with buried corpses. The corpses must be buried in the ground so that the soil can absorb the Vitae.<br /> Once activated the Corpses rise from their graves, filled with hunger and or a simple command towards a target or goal.<br /> For every success on the activation roll, one corpse will rise. These pseudo Revenants are in perpetual Frenzy,<br /> driving by instinct towards their goal. Treat these as individual tree dot Retainers with access to two dots of physical disciplines<br /> that the vampire must possess as well as consider them Revenants for all other intents and purposes.<br /> They will not attack or interfere with one another but others that come in their way is either obstacle or prey.<br /> This Devotion ends with the next sunset. Any corpse befouled by this devotion is at risk of rising as an actual Revanant<br /> after the effect as if exsanguiniated. It shouldn\u2019t need saying, but this Devotion is a clear masquerade breach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T16:08:34-08:00","id":1170543,"title":"","content":"Are revenants going to hunt for kindreds and diablerize? What happens if they do? Do they get to remain vampire, or do they die on the next sunset?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T16:35:16-08:00","id":1170549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1170415-new-devotion-cry-for-the-hungry-horde?p=1170543#post1170543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are revenants going to hunt for kindreds and diablerize? What happens if they do? Do they get to remain vampire, or do they die on the next sunset?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good question. I'd treat them as close to Draugr with a humanity of 0 that goes about hunting and surviving and whatever the beast wants to do in the moment unless they have a specific command.<br /> I guess as they're newly formed &quot;vampires&quot; they'd rather stay away from normal kindred because they'd be inferior, but i guess it could happen, especially if they group up and you want this to happen in the story. However under normal conditions, amaranth is not a goal of the Beast and doesn't strive to do it in frenzy. So in most instances or always if they commit amaranth, it's because the vampire using the Devotion commands them to commit it.<br /> Although if it happens I guess they can be uplifted if they commit amaranth during the duration of the Devotion. If they get uplifted I say they get a Humanity-stat and it would probably start at 6 because of the just begotten amaranth. If this happens as part of story i would not call for a breaking point or humanity loss for that for the vampire that inflicts the Devotion but surely would if that was a stated command. <br /> <br /> So the short story, whatever the story would need, but I'd say yes they become regular kindred but they usually don't go for vampire souls unless commanded to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}